      "narrative": null,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION\nIMPLEMENTATION\nSTRATEGY\nTRACEABILITY\nARCHITECTURE\nANNEXES\nCOUNTRY EXAMPLES\nVital information such as order details, shipping details \nand inventory data must be exchanged among partners in \nthe supply chain to enable seamless movement of health \nproducts. Fig. 2 depicts the flow of information across supply \nchain processes to support the streamlined delivery of health \nproducts. As supply chains become increasingly complex, \ninvolving diverse global and local partners overseeing \ndistinct processes, comprehensive digital transformation \nbecomes essential. \nSupply chain processes",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduction (page 2) presenting Fig. 2 on information flow across supply chain processes, outlining key challenges of manual data entry and siloed systems (stockouts, lack of real-time visibility, administrative burdens, and limited stakeholder collaboration), and defining digital health and the digital health supply chain (DHSC) in alignment with WHO's Global Strategy on Digital Health 2020–2025 and the Classification of Digital Interventions, Services and Applications in Health (Category 3.2).",
